<p>Apple has <a href="https://9to5mac.com/2026/10/08/apple-announces-special-event-for-october-13-welcome-home/">announced</a> that it’s planning something for October 13. The assumption—amplified by the “Welcome Home” slogan—is that Apple is going to roll out a bunch of new home-oriented products, most notably a touchscreen home hub that’s been rumored for a couple of years now.</p>
<p>The word broke <a href="https://x.com/gregjoz/status/2108226096407994858">via an X post by Greg Joswiak</a>. Video creator Marques Brownlee <a href="https://x.com/MKBHD/status/2108226481209934307">posted his invitation</a> to an “Apple Experience” in Tribeca on October 13 at 9am Eastern.</p>
<p>My understanding is that the “experience” at Apple’s cozy building in Tribeca will focus on creators, while some other traditional press will just receive remote briefings. So I think it’s wrong to say there will be an Apple Event next Tuesday. More likely, there will be a 9am Eastern drop of a video and a bunch of press releases. Followed shortly by a bunch of influencer videos shot in Apple’s building, of course.</p>
